## Public data: required attribution

Quill serves records from Government of Canada open datasets that are published
under the Open Government Licence – Canada. Reproduction of those records must
carry this statement:

> Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence – Canada.

Licence: <https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada>

French form: `Contient de l'information visée par la Licence du gouvernement
ouvert – Canada.`

Where a dataset declares the Open Data Licence Agreement of the Office of the
Commissioner of Lobbying, reproduction must carry:

> Contains information licensed under the Open Data Licence Agreement — Office of the Commissioner of Lobbying.

Licence: <https://lobbycanada.gc.ca/en/open-data/open-data-licence-agreement/>

Where a record comes from Statistics Canada, reproduction must carry:

> Source: Statistics Canada, name of product, reference date. Reproduced and
> distributed on an "as is" basis with the permission of Statistics Canada.

Adapted products use: `Adapted from Statistics Canada, name of product,
reference date. This does not constitute an endorsement by Statistics Canada of
this product.`

Licence: <https://www.statcan.gc.ca/en/reference/licence>

