## Parliamentary copyright

The House of Commons and the Senate of Canada each reserve copyright in their
proceedings. Each House grants a limited permission to reproduce. The
permissions are not open licences and they exclude commercial use.

**House of Commons — Speaker's Permission** (<https://www.ourcommons.ca/en/important-notices>):

> Reproduction of the proceedings of the House of Commons and its Committees, in
> whole or in part and in any medium, is hereby permitted provided that the
> reproduction is accurate and is not presented as official. This permission does
> not extend to reproduction, distribution or use for commercial purpose of
> financial gain. [...] All copyrights therein are also reserved.

**Senate of Canada — Permission Regarding Reproduction** (<https://sencanada.ca/en/intellectual-property>):

> Reproduction of the proceedings of the Senate and its committees, in whole or in
> part and in any medium, is hereby permitted provided that the reproduction is not
> presented as official and is accurate [...] This permission does not extend to
> any use for purposes of financial gain. [...] All copyrights of the proceedings
> of the Senate and its committees are also reserved.

Non-commercial reproduction of Senate material must name the Senate as author,
include the title, and link the original. Commercial redistribution is prohibited
without written permission from the Senate.

Quill enforces these limits in code. Sources with `commercialUse: false` are
discovery-only in every tier: metadata, short factual summaries, and links to the
official source. The policy table is
[`packages/pipeline-core/src/shared/source-policy.ts`](./packages/pipeline-core/src/shared/source-policy.ts)
and the CI gate is
[`scripts/gates/check-source-compliance.mjs`](./scripts/gates/check-source-compliance.mjs).

## Federal law

Enactments, consolidations, and the decisions of federally constituted courts and
administrative tribunals may be reproduced under the *Reproduction of Federal Law
Order* (SI/97-5)
(<https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SI-97-5/FullText.html>):

> Anyone may, without charge or request for permission, reproduce enactments and
> consolidations of enactments of the Government of Canada, and decisions and
> reasons for decisions of federally-constituted courts and administrative
> tribunals, provided due diligence is exercised in ensuring the accuracy of the
> materials reproduced and the reproduction is not represented as an official
> version.

Every record that comes from this class of source carries a "not an official
version" notice at the service boundary.

## Personal information

The Open Government Licence – Canada and the lobbying open data licence grant no
right to use personal information. A dataset can contain individuals' names and
still not license that personal information. The Statistics Canada Open Licence
also prohibits merging or linking information to identify an individual person,
business, or organization. Quill minimises personal contact fields at the service
boundary. Send correction or removal requests to privacy@maplespike.ca.

